WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.611
You have a note to turn into a message
before the next job.

2
00:00:05.611 --> 00:00:09.851
An AI helper can draft it, organise it or
shorten it.

3
00:00:09.851 --> 00:00:13.320
In this course, every farm and document is
fictional.

4
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.560
You will practise with Example Station and
check the result yourself.

5
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.919
The note says a gate hinge needs
inspection.

6
00:00:21.919 --> 00:00:25.923
Tuesday has been requested, but no visit
is booked.

7
00:00:25.923 --> 00:00:28.147
Give the helper those facts.

8
00:00:28.147 --> 00:00:33.931
Ask for a short contractor enquiry, and
tell it to leave unknown details

9
00:00:33.931 --> 00:00:34.376
visible.

10
00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:36.600
That instruction is your prompt.

11
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:41.205
The answer may look useful and still
change the meaning.

12
00:00:41.205 --> 00:00:47.293
If it says the contractor will arrive at
eight on Tuesday, it has added a time

13
00:00:47.293 --> 00:00:48.434
and a commitment.

14
00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.337
Neither appears in the note.

15
00:00:50.337 --> 00:00:53.000
Smooth wording cannot supply that missing
evidence.

16
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.134
Replace the promise with a question about
availability.

17
00:00:57.134 --> 00:01:00.885
Then compare the revised draft with the
note again.

18
00:01:00.885 --> 00:01:03.385
Check names, dates, quantities and
commitments.

19
00:01:03.385 --> 00:01:06.302
If there is a number, recalculate it.

20
00:01:06.302 --> 00:01:11.720
If there is a citation, open the source
and read the supporting words.

21
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.834
Begin with a small task you can check.

22
00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:20.804
Keep health, spraying and legal decisions
with the responsible person and the

23
00:01:20.804 --> 00:01:21.633
relevant evidence.

24
00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:25.361
You can complete this course without an AI
account.

25
00:01:25.361 --> 00:01:30.332
The local activities give you invented
drafts to review, and paper practice

26
00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:31.160
works too.

27
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.816
Next, try spotting added details in an AI
draft.

28
00:01:35.816 --> 00:01:40.957
Tap what the original notes do not
support, then read the explanation.

29
00:01:40.957 --> 00:01:46.527
If you use voice input later, practise
while parked and check the transcript

30
00:01:46.527 --> 00:01:47.384
before sending.

31
00:01:47.384 --> 00:01:51.240
A noisy recording can change a date or
number.
